From: Galaxy Book 12 Linux contributors
Subject: [PATCH] media: ipu-bridge: add Galaxy Book 12 IMX258

The Samsung Galaxy Book 12 exposes its rear Sony IMX258 as SONY258A.
Without an entry in ipu_supported_sensors, ipu-bridge does not attach the
software-node graph and imx258 probe fails with "Endpoint node not found".

The patched IMX258 driver provides the established 633.6 and 320 MHz link
frequency menu for the tablet's 26 MHz reference clock.

--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
@@ -97,6 +97,8 @@ static const struct ipu_sensor_config ipu_supported_sensors[] = {
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("OVTI8856", 3, 180000000, 360000000, 720000000),
+	/* Sony IMX258 (Samsung Galaxy Book 12) */
+	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("SONY258A", 2, 633600000, 320000000),
 	/* Sony IMX471 */
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("SONY471A", 1, 200000000),
 	/* Toshiba T4KA3 */
